From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:44:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0306r: an owner's reminder may name a day up to 60 days ahead
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's FAIL (box 61805): „remind me on 28 Oct" was set for 23 Oct and
the owner was told „this is not 28 Oct" — honest, but not what was asked.
A reminder is one row the server delivers at its time; the week cap was a
goal wake's, not a reminder's. Reminders now reach up to 60 days (minutes
1–86400; a named day up to 60 days ahead). A goal's wake keeps its week.

The set_reminder description changes with it (7 -> 60 days, 10080 ->
86400, day_offset up to 60): model-facing, so HELD for Misho's yes (D44).

